{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/713153-possible-for-ex-pentex-employees-from-any-subsidiary-to-fight-back-against-them","id":713153,"title":"Possible for ex-Pentex employees(from any Subsidiary) to fight back against them?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-21T16:18:28-07:00","id":713153,"title":"Possible for ex-Pentex employees(from any Subsidiary) to fight back against them?","content":"Say a former employee who decides for whatever reason to wage a war against them...<br /> <br /> Maybe he/she was experimented on, did a number of jobs for them, or even was a member of First Team. Something happens(or a number of things happen) and this former soldier/scientist/lab experiment of Pentex breaks away from them to start their own crusade.<br /> <br /> Is that possible? Has anyone ever played such a character in a game? Anyone ever have such a character as an NPC in a game? Is this a stupid idea?<br /> <br /> How do you think Werewolves would react to such a character?<br /> <br /> My apologies if this has been answered before, as I'm still getting used to the setting.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T16:40:55-07:00","id":713181,"title":"","content":"sure its possible. i doubt werewolves would trust them in the least because it seems like a trick, but if they pulled something big the garou might decide to ignore them. if they are bane possessed or particularly tainted than i doubt they would be able to rebel in the first place, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7141-nasrudin","name":"Nasrudin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T19:46:36-07:00","id":713524,"title":"","content":"Yes, but it's incredibly difficult. The only reason that one guy from Magadon manages to do it on his own is because of all of the anti-agathics keeping him young with his decades of experience in numerous fields. So, basically, you'd need people with extreme coordination and decades of experience in multiple fields of importance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T04:16:21-07:00","id":714135,"title":"","content":"It's certainly possible, but it's also going to be a very dangerous, very difficult, and presumably very rare thing. One issue is that most employees of Pentex work for a subsidiary, not the big company itself, and often will have no idea at all that there's a much bigger beast out there. So while an Endron oil guy might stumble into a Glade and have a spiritual awakening that leads him to a one-man terrorist crusade on oil refineries, etc, he's probably not going to put two and two together and also start blowing up Magadon warehouses - he might suss out Harold and Harold or Ardus Enterprises, but will probably be relatively myopic. In this regard, he's no different than the Garou, who are typically presented as only vaguely aware of this company called Pentex and have no clue just how big it is and how deep its tendrils have curled into the Western economic system.<br /> <br /> He's probably going to be torn apart by werewolves, since there's a strong chance any such employee will read as Wyrm-ish to one degree or another. If they find him blowing up a warehouse they might be inclined to stop and listen, and his best bet when it comes to clemency and getting help from the Garou would be to run to the Glass Walkers, Bone Gnawers, or Children of Gaia (good luck figuring them out from the outside, though.) That could make a very tense session, actually - a request from a BG/GW caern to rescue a whistleblower from inside a Pentex-run 'detox center' without getting him killed in the process.<br /> <br /> It's a solid idea for an NPC if used with a bit of thought and without being too common. If you use a cross-over setting and don't mind supernaturals being more common, a First Teamer or Pentex employee becoming Imbued could be one hell of a plotline and wild card (and wouldn't be that unlikely, either, as the imbued tend to be those who encounter the supernatural more often than the norm and who have the potential to do great damage to it at some point in their future; a rogue Pentex scientist waking up when he sees a bane and fleeing with documents that could topple the whole company certainly fits, as does a First Team member who suddenly gains the ability to see Garou even when they're not shapeshifted into Crinos...), and would have the kind of personal fortitude and abilities to let them survive long enough to serve as an antagonist or ally.<br /> <br /> The next nWoD game may also give you some good ideas. Deviant will deal with somewhat similar subject matter (test subjects, scientists gone wrong, etc) so it may have stuff to harvest, but it won't be out for quite a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T06:18:29-07:00","id":714298,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the replies, everyone. It's actually helped me a lot. Might be playing a game(as a player, not an ST) in the future where this may be allowed--either as a player character or NPC.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T06:30:47-07:00","id":714342,"title":"","content":"One thing to remember. Most employees of Pentex subsidiaries are normal people. They come from all walkways of life and have a million different professions, hobies and fixations. Most of them are not Wyrm corrupted. Most of them are not fomori. Most of them have no bloody idea their companies have SECRET projects that seek to mutilate humanity and murder the world. This kind of employees can be easily let go as they are no risk to the company. Just another cog in the grand machine<br /> <br /> People who actually know what's going on are more likely to be vetted and controlled, because any kind of leaks on Pentex activities are horribly dangerous. The really nasty shit they do would cost them a shitload of money and reputation. So even if your morals are on the level and you want to do the right thing, you may not have a choice once their hooks are in you. If you run and know something you shouldn't, remember that they own you. They know you. And they're coming for you no matter who they have to bribe, intimidate, butcher or brainwash to get to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T08:17:04-07:00","id":714601,"title":"","content":"One of the books has an example detailing the lengths that Pentex goes to create the perfect employee. I like the idea of a poor working guy being a whistle blower, who is on the run from Pentex. A late change Garou, a suddenly imbued Hunter, or even a human with a numina allowing him to &quot;see&quot; would all work. Especially with Secrets or Destiny backgrounds or perhaps the dark fate flaw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T13:51:33-07:00","id":715360,"title":"","content":"Any idea how long it will be before pentex employee indoctrination guide is out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}